<title>CHINA: China to set up grain bases to boost production.</title>
<headline>China to set up grain bases to boost production.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>China plans to set up 20 large commodity grain production bases in major grain-producing provinces, the Xinhua news agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>When completed, the 20 production bases are expected to yield an additional 10 million tonnes of grain output a year, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>By the year 2000, the bases will turn out 90 million tonnes of grain, accounting for 18 percent of China's total, Xinhua said, but gave no other details.</p>
<p>Officials have forecast a harvest of 480 million tonnnes of grain for this year, up from a record 466 million last year.</p>
</text>
